WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.1 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
MEAL principles and a proportionate system

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
MEAL tells you, from day one, whether you are doing what you said and what to change.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
MEAL stands for Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning. It is a light system that tells you whether you are doing what you said, whether it makes a difference and what to change.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Four parts, four questions

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.241
Monitoring: Tracks, regularly, what you are doing and what is changing. For example: A sheet filled in at every repair session: who came and what was fixed.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:47.719
Evaluation: Asks whether it made a difference, for whom and why. For example: A short end-of-pilot review: are families still repairing things at home?

7
00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:58.678
Accountability: The people you serve can shape the work and raise concerns safely. For example: A feedback card at each session, plus a trusted outsider for sensitive concerns.

8
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:09.726
Learning: Turns what you found into decisions for the next round. For example: After the pilot, three decisions: new times, more tools, a second venue.

9
00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:10.726
Why start it now

10
00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:16.400
1. You have evidence from day one instead of reconstructing it later.

11
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.074
2. You find out early whether your idea works, before you grow.

12
00:01:22.074 --> 00:01:28.007
3. Funders, customers and members trust results they can see.

13
00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:29.007
What it builds

14
00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:34.311
1. One chain: Theory of Change, results, indicators, data, learning, decisions.

15
00:01:34.311 --> 00:01:39.985
2. Each lesson in this module adds one link to that chain.

16
00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:46.289
3. Your reports, proof points and communications draw on it later.

17
00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:47.289
What to avoid

18
00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:52.222
Collecting data you will never use for a decision.

19
00:01:52.222 --> 00:01:57.896
Fifty indicators nobody reviews instead of three to five good ones.

20
00:01:57.896 --> 00:02:04.570
Waiting for tablets or databases: paper sheets and photos are enough.

21
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.970
You write your MEAL purpose and the decisions it must inform.

22
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:10.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
